-- title:
--   A token lower bound with the paid endpoint residue
-- statement:
--   Write $I_n=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, with cyclic arithmetic modulo $n$ and integer representatives for inequalities; $[x]_n$ denotes the least nonnegative residue when $n>0$. For an integer board $d:I_n\to\mathbb Z$, put $F_i=i+d_i$, $\lambda_i=F_i\bmod n$, $C_{ij}=-\lfloor(((j-i)\bmod n)+d_j-d_i)/n\rfloor$, $B_i=\sum_j\max(-C_{ij},0)$, and $I(d)=\sum_{i<j}|\lfloor(F_j-F_i)/n\rfloor|$. A balanced lift of a permutation $p$ with phase $c$ means $\sum_i d_i=0$ and $i+d_i\equiv p^{-1}(i)+c\pmod n$. A greedy scan compares the first two integer targets, exchanges a strict descent, and otherwise advances the cyclic cursor, stopping at the zero board. For its trace $g$, write $P_c(g)=\#_L(g)+((c-\#_L(g))\bmod n)$ for the paid rotation count. Let $n\ge2$, let $d$ lift $p$ with phase $c\in I_n$, and let $g$ be a greedy trace. If $[x]_n$ denotes the representative in $I_n$ and $(i-1)_+=\max(i-1,0)$, then
--
--   $$
--   n(i-1)_+-(n-1)F_i+[-p^{-1}(i)]_n\le P_c(g).
--   $$
--
--   The endpoint residue strengthens the cursor budget for each individual token.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean/blob/8cddcd222b591673dc63475d9d45b9ed5c6eb92c/LX/AntipodeBoundaryPhase.lean#L11-L45

